# User-uploaded artifacts. These are end-user content served back over
# GET /api/v1/software-management/storage/download/{storage_key}, not source.
# Tracking them puts arbitrary uploaded files (including .py) into version
# control.
#
# Anchored to the repository root. An unanchored ``storage/`` matches a
# directory of that name at *any* depth, which silently swallowed
# ``app/infrastructure/storage/`` -- so ``local_artifact_stager.py`` was never
# committed and a fresh clone could not import the application.
# ``app/infrastructure/storage/`` -- a source directory, not this one.
/storage/

